{
  "set": "phase-1-org",
  "note": [
    "Phase 1 of Sales_Comp_Design_Walkthrough.md - who gets paid - as real records.",
    "",
    "The people, seats and titles are the ChargePoint personas the Sales Commission",
    "Management app already renders from app/src/data/org-seed.ts, so the backend and",
    "the app's screens describe the same organisation rather than two different ones.",
    "The STRUCTURE is the walkthrough's: identity separate from seat, seat separate",
    "from what the seat is, and every one of those dated.",
    "",
    "EDGE CASES ARE DELIBERATE. Each one below is a rule from the walkthrough made",
    "real, so a reader can see the model earn its keep instead of taking it on faith:",
    "",
    "  1  POS-W-AE-09 is VACANT - a seat that exists and has a title but has never",
    "     been assigned. Deals in its territory still credit to it; that is the",
    "     'unfilled seats with revenue' report, and without seats they'd be errors.",
    "  2  POS-W-AE-09 also OMITS `active` entirely. A boolean never set is MISSING,",
    "     not false - anything reading it with a truthiness test is wrong, and this",
    "     row is what proves it.",
    "  3  POS-E-AE-07 goes vacant MID-YEAR: David Okoye was terminated 2026-05-30 and",
    "     his assignment ends there. Ask who held that seat in March and the answer is",
    "     David; ask for June and the honest answer is nobody.",
    "  4  Sofia Almeida MOVES SEATS: SDR until 2026-06-30, then a new AE seat from",
    "     2026-07-01. Two non-overlapping rows, never an edit. Her March statement is",
    "     an SDR's, her August one an AE's, and neither changed the other.",
    "  5  POS-W-AE-04 is PROMOTED mid-year - AE to Enterprise AE on 2026-07-01 - as a",
    "     second PositionAttribute row. March still resolves to the AE plan.",
    "  6  POS-EU-AE-05 has its TERRITORY RE-CUT at the half-year, same mechanism, and",
    "     shows that a title can stay put while a territory moves.",
    "  7  POS-GBL-VP-01 has NO territoryId at all (a global seat) and NO",
    "     PositionHierarchy row. The missing hierarchy row is how the rollup walk",
    "     knows it has reached the top and stops.",
    "  8  POS-EU-AE-08 did not exist before 2026-07-01 and has no attribute row before",
    "     then. A seat with no attribute on a date cannot resolve a plan, and the",
    "     pre-check must say so rather than guess.",
    "  9  POS-AP-SDR-01 is RE-ORGed: it reported to the APAC RSM until 2026-03-31 and",
    "     to the EMEA RSM from 2026-04-01. A March deal rolls up to Kenji, an April",
    "     one to Michael, with nothing else changed.",
    " 10  Liam Patel is ON_LEAVE and STILL HOLDS his seat. Leave is a payee status,",
    "     not a vacancy - the seat is not open and must not be filled.",
    " 11  Three currencies with per-period FX. A rate is a fact about a currency AND a",
    "     point in time, so it lives on FxRate; on Currency it would silently",
    "     recalculate March at today's rate.",
    " 12  The calendar carries all three writability states: JAN-2026 PAID, FEB-2026",
    "     CLOSED, MAR-2026 OPEN. `ICM | Check Period Writable` should answer WRITABLE",
    "     for exactly one of them. Q1-2026 is still OPEN because a quarter cannot lock",
    "     until every month in it has.",
    " 13  SPIF is an INACTIVE credit type - retired, kept for history, unusable in new",
    "     rules.",
    " 14  No Payee carries a userId. None of these people is a platform user yet, and",
    "     an optional FK left empty is the normal state, not a gap to paper over.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: no overlapping assignment for one seat, no",
    "overlapping seat for one person, no hierarchy cycle. Those are the states the",
    "pre-check must REFUSE, and seeding them would put invalid data in production to",
    "make a point. They belong in a regression suite against KITFIX- fixtures on",
    "orbit, where deleting them afterwards is safe.",
    "",
    "NOT YET REPRESENTABLE: the walkthrough puts `target_incentive` on",
    "PayeePositionAssignment - what a person earns at 100% attainment, dated because",
    "it is agreed per person per seat. The schema has no such field, so no assignment",
    "below carries one."
  ],
